# Which UCLA ROMS namelist vocabulary each roms_gpu release reads.
#
# A release reads the namelist groups and keys of the UCLA ROMS release named
# here, plus its own optional groups below. Groups it does not read are
# ignored; a CPU feature switch it does not have stops the run at start-up
# (src/host/feature_guard.F90). From v0.1.2-beta, a key it does not know in a
# group it reads stops the run at start-up, naming the group (before, the rest
# of that group silently kept its defaults).
#
# Keys added in later UCLA ROMS releases that roms_gpu reads (after
# v0.1.3-beta; before, a namelist with them stopped at the read):
#   0.12.0  &cdr_lite_settings  cdr_carbonate_sensitivity_time_interpolation
#           as UCLA ROMS: .true. (default) interpolates ddic_dco2 and
#           ddic_dalk linearly in time; .false. holds each record until the
#           model time passes the next one (the first step of a run takes
#           the record at or before its time), without the missing-record
#           rule (the CPU applies it only with interpolation).
#   0.13.0  &v_sponge_settings  v_sponge_trc
#           as UCLA ROMS: the maximum tracer diffusivity of the sponge
#           layer (m^2/s); negative or absent: v_sponge; 0: a sponge on the
#           currents only. Every tracer (T, S, the passive, CDR_LITE and
#           MARBL tracers) gets it. v_sponge = 0 with v_sponge_trc > 0
#           gives a sponge on the tracers only. Output files carry the
#           global attributes v_sponge, v_sponge_trc and their _units, as
#           UCLA ROMS.
#
# Keys of UCLA ROMS after 0.14.0 (dev) that roms_gpu reads, so that a
# namelist written from its template runs:
#   &bgc_settings  bgc_physics_subcycle, bgc_physics_timestep (BGC tracer
#     subcycling, #428 and #430), and its testing keys bgc_subcycle_pos and
#     bgc_subcycle_diag; supported values and refusals in the BGC tracer
#     subcycling section below.
#   &marbl_biogeochemistry_settings  marbl_balance (#430), which ships MARBL
#     columns between CPU ranks and changes no result. Each GPU computes
#     the wet columns of its tile (&tile_settings balances them), so
#     .true. is ignored, with a start-up note.
#   &imex_igw_settings  the IMEX internal-wave step and its 'modal' open
#     boundary (#433, #434); keys and accepted values in the IMEX section
#     below. Required in every namelist, with its switch imex_igw (ucla-roms
#     PR for the imex_igw key, branch imex-igw-key).
#
# GPU-only additions: the optional groups &tile_settings (tile balancing),
# &periodic_settings (periodicity, below), &passive_tracers (n_passive,
# init_mode, write_passive), and in &param_settings the key n. Removed
# after v0.1.3-beta (unused; a namelist that sets them now stops at the
# read): &param_settings nsub_x, nsub_e and ntrc_bio (not UCLA ROMS keys),
# &bgc_settings nbgc_flx (UCLA ROMS still reads it, unused, and its
# template does not set it). The GPU-only groups
# &flux_frc_settings and &bulk_frc_settings (unused copies of
# &surf_frc_settings keys) are no longer read, so they are ignored.
#
# UCLA ROMS settings that roms_gpu reads but cannot honour stop the run at
# start-up with a message naming the key (after v0.1.3-beta; before, they
# were ignored or, for diag_uv and diag_trc, gave a warning):
#   &ts_output_settings        wrt_temp_dia, wrt_salt_dia = .true.
#   &diagnostics_settings      diag_uv, diag_trc = .true.
#   &surf_flx_output_settings  wrt_swflx = .true.
#   &bgc_settings              wrt_bgc_dia_his = .true. (no _bgc_dia file;
#                              wrt_bgc_dia_avg = .true. already stopped)
#   &implicit_fs               fs_selftest > 0 with fs_mode = 'implicit'
#                              (UCLA ROMS runs the self-test only there)
#   &marbl_biogeochemistry_settings
#     marbl_diagnostics_to_write: a name outside the fixed set the GPU
#     writes to _his (PH, pCO2SURF, DpCO2, FG_CO2, FG_ALT_CO2, PH_ALT_CO2,
#     pCO2SURF_ALT_CO2, zsatcalc, zsatarag, CO3, CO3_ALT_CO2,
#     co3_sat_calc, co3_sat_arag). An empty list (UCLA ROMS: all) is
#     accepted. On UCLA ROMS the list selects the _bgc_dia files' fields.
#     marbl_config_file: a non-empty name of a file that does not exist
#     (before, the GPU ran MARBL with its default settings); "" runs MARBL
#     with its defaults, as UCLA ROMS. The path is relative to the
#     namelist file.
#
# &nhmg_settings nhmg = .true. stops the run at start-up: roms_gpu has no
# non-hydrostatic solver. (UCLA ROMS from its run-time NHMG switch,
# unreleased; before, NHMG was a cpp key the GPU could not see.)
#
# &surf_frc_settings check_bulk_frc_units = .true. (after v0.1.3-beta;
# before, ignored): as UCLA ROMS, with bulk forcing, after the first step's
# fluxes the units attribute of qair must be 'kg/kg' and of rain 'cm/day'
# in the file of the record read last; otherwise the run stops. No effect
# with flux forcing.
#
# Averages of temperature and salinity: &ts_output_settings wrt_avg_temp
# and wrt_avg_salt (default .false., as UCLA ROMS) put temp and salt in the
# _avg file. As on UCLA ROMS, with MARBL the tracers selected by
# marbl_tracers_to_write are averaged too: an empty list (every tracer) or
# a list naming temp or salt averages them whatever wrt_avg_temp and
# wrt_avg_salt say. Before, the GPU averaged T and S only through that
# list (without MARBL, never), which the default .false. keeps.
#
# Atmospheric xCO2 for MARBL: &bgc_settings xco2air_default (ppm, default
# 284.7) is used where the forcing files hold no xco2_air (xco2_air_alt
# for the ALT_CO2 system), as UCLA ROMS without PCO2AIR_FORCING. Before,
# the GPU read the key and used a fixed 284.7.
#
# Default change (after v0.1.3-beta): &tile_settings tile_land_weight, the
# cost of a land cell against a wet cell in the default 'wet' tile balance,
# now defaults by run: 0.10 with MARBL (nt_bgc > 0, as before), 0.35
# without MARBL (was 0.10), including runs with only generic or CDR_LITE
# passive tracers. A value >= 0 in the namelist is used as given; a start-up
# line ('tiles: land weight ... from ...') names the weight and its source.
# A multi-tile 'wet' run without MARBL and without the key gets new tile
# cuts; tile_land_weight = 0.10 keeps the old ones.
#
# Periodic grids: the optional GPU-only group &periodic_settings with the
# logicals ew_periodic, ns_periodic (UCLA ROMS sets the same with its cpp
# keys EW_PERIODIC and NS_PERIODIC, param.F90 ew_periodic / ns_periodic,
# and ignores the group, so one namelist serves both models). Group
# absent: the periodicity is inferred from the grid file's size as before
# (LLm+2 x MMm+2 closed, LLm x MMm doubly periodic), and a start-up line
# names it. Group present: it sets the periodicity (a key left out is
# .false.; one direction may be periodic alone), and the grid file and
# the initial or
# restart file are each checked against it: a closed direction needs
# LLm+2 (MMm+2) rho points; a periodic one takes UCLA ROMS's layout,
# LLm+2 with the periodic copies as first and last points (only the
# interior is read), or roms_gpu's LLm (MMm). Any other size stops the
# run with the expected sizes. Output files keep roms_gpu's layout (no
# boundary points in a periodic direction), which UCLA ROMS cannot read.
#
# &rho0_settings rho0: read at run time and required, as in UCLA ROMS (a
# namelist without the group stops the run). Up to v0.1.3-beta roms_gpu fixed
# rho0 at build time (-DROMS_RHO0, default 1000) and stopped when the
# namelist differed.
#
# Surface restoring: UCLA ROMS selects it with cpp keys, which the GPU model
# cannot see; roms_gpu switches it on with logical keys in
# &surf_frc_settings (default .false., bulk forcing only), and reads the
# coefficient from the same group as UCLA ROMS. UCLA ROMS (after 0.16.0,
# ucla-roms#475) also accepts these three keys and stops when one
# disagrees with its cpp key, so a namelist can carry them for both models:
#   CPU cpp key        roms_gpu &surf_frc_settings   coefficient group (cm/day)
#   SFLX_CORR          sflx_corr = .true.             &sss_correction dSSSdt
#   QCORRECTION        qcorrection = .true.           &sst_correction dSSTdt
#   CFLX_CORR (MARBL)  cflx_corr = .true.             &dic_alk_correction dCdt
# A forcing file holding the restoring data (sss, sst, sDIC/sALK)
# while its switch is off gives a start-up warning. The restoring-flux
# output (&surf_flx_output_settings wrt_rstflx) is not on the GPU.
#
# Pressure fluxes for nesting: &calc_pflx_settings calc_pflx and
# pflx_timescale as UCLA ROMS (the group is optional here; absent means
# off). Both models compute up/vp whenever calc_pflx = .true. (UCLA ROMS
# up to 0.16.0 only when built with the DIAGNOSTICS cpp key); roms_gpu
# uses the internal-tide pressure of ucla-roms eae883ee, writes up_<side>/vp_<side>
# to the child boundary file for objects whose output_vars name them, and
# keeps u_slow, v_slow, p_slow in the restart. pflx_timescale must be > 0
# when calc_pflx is on (the run stops otherwise).
#
# Sponge tuning for nested children: &sponge_tune_settings ub_tune (the CPU
# needs the SPONGE_TUNE cpp key as well; the GPU only the switch) tunes the
# inflow nudging of the open boundaries to the parent's up/vp of the
# boundary files; it needs calc_pflx = .true. (the run stops otherwise), as
# UCLA ROMS. wrt_sponge writes <output_root_name>_spn.<date>.nc every
# output_period_sponge (nrpf_sponge records per file): the child and parent
# fluxes and the coefficient of every open side, averaged over the period
# (sponge_avg) or of the output step, as UCLA ROMS with its fixes of
# 2026-11 (sponge-tune-pio-fixes). As UCLA ROMS's precheck, with restarts
# and wrt_sponge on, nrpf_sponge * output_period_sponge must be positive
# and divide output_period_rst (the run stops otherwise). The coefficients
# ub_west, ub_east, ub_south, ub_north are restart fields, written after
# the step's tuning (exact restarts), as in that version of UCLA ROMS.
#
# Implicit free surface (&implicit_fs, fs_mode = 'implicit'; absent or
# 'split': the split-explicit fast loop), as in ucla-roms
# implicit-fs-defaults. The settings (the five keys of UCLA ROMS's
# namelist template; defaults in brackets):
#   fs_mode     'split' | 'implicit'                                ['split']
#   fs_nsub     implicit sub-steps of dt/fs_nsub per step, 1..4     [2]
#   fs_rho_inf  spectral radius at infinite omega dt, in [0, 1)     [0.5]
#               (1, Crank-Nicolson, stops the run at the read)
#   fs_tol      relative residual of the elliptic solve             [1e-8]
#   fs_verbose  1: FS_SOLVE line per step; 2: + FS_VOL, FS_SRC,      [0]
#               FS_WALL lines (FS_SRC also with fs_mode = 'split')
# Solver and development settings: read as in UCLA ROMS, where the
# defaults are the recommended values, the keys may change between
# versions and C-Star and Forge do not expose them: fs_theta,
# fs_theta_div, fs_maxit (a solve that reaches it without meeting fs_tol
# stops the run), fs_precond, fs_mg_levels, fs_mg_nu, fs_mg_smoother,
# fs_mg_lag, fs_mg_faces, fs_drag_implicit, fs_warm, fs_tang_nudge,
# fs_cor_metric, fs_pot_time, fs_pg_rho, fs_flather_zghost (fs_rho_inf =
# 0, fs_nsub = 1, fs_pg_rho = fs_flather_zghost = .false. give the earlier
# single step); UCLA ROMS's MPI-layout keys fs_mg_gather, fs_mg_global_on
# and fs_exch_thin are read and not used; fs_selftest > 0 stops the run
# (the GPU has no solver self-test).
# GPU tuning settings (roms_gpu only): fs_gpu_gather, fs_gpu_coarse,
# fs_gpu_graph and fs_gpu_opt (layout and latency of the solve),
# fs_gpu_timers (timing runs: FS_COST, FS_WIN). fs_stress_time is no
# longer read (as in UCLA ROMS): a namelist that sets it stops at the
# read. Output files record fs_mode, and with 'implicit' fs_rho_inf and
# fs_nsub, as global attributes.
# Boundary options: roms_gpu's open edges have one barotropic type, UCLA
# ROMS's OBC_M2FLATHER (Flather normal faces, the zetabc sea level, the
# upwind tangential condition with inflow nudging), which the implicit
# free surface implements. The UCLA ROMS options for which the implicit
# step prints a start-up note there (OBC_M2ORLANSKI, open edges without an
# OBC_M2 type, OBC_Z2ORLANSKI, LEGACY_ORLANSKI, OBC_RAD_NORMAL, OBC_RAD_NPO)
# do not exist in roms_gpu, so it prints none.
# fs_gpu_opt is a bit mask in [0, 65535], default 65495 (was 471: bits
# 512 .. 32768 are new); bit 512 sums the PCG's partials of four ranks on
# one node in pairwise order instead of by MPI_Allreduce (GPU-only
# rounding-level difference; it applies to the PCG of the IMEX step as
# well, also with fs_mode = 'split'), every other bit is bit-identical to 0. The
# solve stops the run on a NaN or Inf residual norm or <p,q>, with the
# CPU's message.
#
# BGC tracer subcycling (&bgc_settings; ucla-roms #428 and #430): the
# BGC tracers (every tracer after temperature and salinity) are
# transported, mixed and forced once per window from the transports summed
# over the window, as UCLA ROMS does it, with its checks, restart rule and
# start-up messages. Keys (defaults in brackets):
#   bgc_physics_subcycle  .true. subcycles the BGC tracers             [.false.]
#   bgc_physics_timestep  window length in s; a whole multiple of dt,      [0]
#                         and with MARBL it must divide marbl_timestep
#                         (MARBL runs at the end of a window); 0 =
#                         marbl_timestep; > 0 is required without MARBL
#   bgc_subcycle_diag     0 none; 1 the BGCSUB / BGCSUBNEG window lines    [0]
#                         (Courant numbers, sub-passes, continuity,
#                         shadow tracer, per-tracer budget, new
#                         negatives); >= 2 is refused (see below)
#   bgc_subcycle_pos      only .false. (the positivity limiter is      [.false.]
#                         refused, see below)
# Restarts only on window boundaries: with subcycling, output_period_rst
# must be a multiple of the window and the run must start on a window
# boundary (the time step of the initial file a multiple of the window in
# steps); monthly_restarts is not on the GPU at all. A window length that
# is shorter than dt, not a whole multiple of dt, or does not divide
# marbl_timestep stops the run, naming the nearest valid lengths.
# Subcycled as on the CPU: rivers (including river faces in the 2-point
# halo of a tile), CDR releases in all four modes (parameterized tracer
# fluxes, volume releases, depth profiles, 3D forcing), the CDR_LITE and
# CFLX_CORR surface fluxes, any number of passive tracers, with or
# without MARBL, split or implicit free surface, and with the IMEX
# internal-wave step (&imex_igw_settings; 'modal' or 'fixed' open
# boundary), as UCLA ROMS dev 809aa24a runs the combination.
# Refused at start-up (each with its own message): bgc_subcycle_pos =
# .true. and bgc_subcycle_diag >= 2 (the positivity limiter and its test;
# not on the GPU yet); UPSCALING output and ub_tune (refused by UCLA ROMS
# too); the GPU-only &passive_tracers init_mode = 'mirror_salt' test
# tracer; builds without -DPASSIVE_FP64.
#
# IMEX internal-wave step (&imex_igw_settings with imex_igw = .true.), as
# in ucla-roms #433 and #434 (IMEX_IGW with its 'modal' open boundary).
# The group and its logical switch imex_igw are required in every
# namelist, as in UCLA ROMS (ucla-roms PR for the imex_igw key, branch
# imex-igw-key); imex_igw has no default:
#   imex_igw = .true.   IMEX on (UCLA ROMS: needs a build with IMEX_IGW)
#   imex_igw = .false.  the stock step (UCLA ROMS: a build without
#                       IMEX_IGW); the group's other keys are read (an
#                       unknown or removed key still stops the run) and
#                       ignored, with a start-up note that lists them
# A namelist without the group or without the key stops the run at
# start-up with a message naming the key and its two values. The start-up
# log states the setting ('IMEX_IGW: on (imex_igw = .true.)' or
# 'IMEX_IGW: off (imex_igw = .false.)'). A run without IMEX needs only
#   &imex_igw_settings imex_igw = .false. /
# Change (after v0.1.3-beta): up to then the group's presence switched
# IMEX on (the CPU's cpp key IMEX_IGW was the presence of the group), and
# a namelist without it ran the stock step without a log line; add
# imex_igw = .true. to the group of an IMEX run and the line above to a
# namelist without IMEX. The settings (the keys of UCLA ROMS's namelist
# template; defaults in brackets):
#   imex_verbose     0 quiet; 1 solver statistics (IMEX line,           [0]
#                    IMEX_SOLVE); 2 + the true FP64 residual of every
#                    solve (IMEX_PCHK), its residual history (IMEX_RH,
#                    ucla-roms #442: one line per fused stage solve,
#                    none with imex_pcg_start 0, as on the CPU) and
#                    max |dp|; same results
#   imex_bref_hours  rebuild interval (model hours) of the reference     [24]
#                    stratification b_ref, the operator, its
#                    preconditioner and the 'modal' boundary modes; 12
#                    for strongly evolving stratification. The longest
#                    age of b_ref: imex_bref_trigger rebuilds it earlier
#                    where it goes stale
#   imex_rst_state   1 the IMEX state in the restart files (exact        [1]
#                    restart); 0 none (smaller files, inexact restart)
#   imex_obc_mode    normal velocity at open faces: 'modal' the     ['auto']
#                    characteristic (per-mode Flather) condition,
#                    implicit in the stage solves; 'fixed' the OBC's
#                    explicit value; 'auto' 'modal' when an open side
#                    exists and every open side has 3-D boundary data
#                    (normal velocity, temperature, salinity: the CPU's
#                    M3_FRC_BRY and T_FRC_BRY), else 'fixed' (decided at
#                    the first step and printed)
#   imex_obc_tref    'modal': time scale (s) of the reference m(z),  [259200]
#                    the low-passed baroclinic mismatch that is not
#                    radiated; 0 none; >= ~3 inertial periods at the
#                    open edges' lowest |f| and >= 1 d
# Solver and development settings: read as in UCLA ROMS, where the
# defaults are the recommended values, the keys may change between
# versions and C-Star and Forge do not expose them: imex_theta_p,
# imex_phi, imex_theta_c, imex_mu, imex_nu, imex_rho, imex_am3_crv (only
# 1/6 on the GPU), imex_tol_pred, imex_tol_corr, imex_maxit,
# imex_solver_enabled, imex_allow_explicit, imex_selftest (only 0 on the
# GPU), imex_n2_ref, imex_n2_taper, imex_warm (0, 1), imex_setup_lag,
# imex_pcg_start (0, 2, 3 on the GPU: 1 is CPU-only), imex_pcg_fused,
# imex_solver_prec, imex_stage_fused (only 1 on the GPU), imex_redu (only
# 0 on the GPU), imex_mix_split (0, 1), and of the boundary
# imex_obc_nmodes, imex_obc_q0 (0 off, or 0.2-1: sqrt(1 - f^2/omega0^2)
# where f/omega0 > 0.6 at the edges where the internal tide enters),
# imex_obc_cmin, imex_obc_mprint (OBCM/OBCF lines). The values the GPU refuses stop
# the run at start-up. imex_corr_adv (code-only on the CPU as well, not in
# its namelist template; ucla-roms PR for imex_corr_adv, branch
# imex-advective-buoyancy, 746cb6f7 and 6e675129): 1, the default on both
# codes since ucla-roms branch imex-corr-adv-default (0595719e; it was 0
# before), adds the step's advective buoyancy change to the corrector rhs
# (IMEX_ADVB lines at imex_verbose 2); 0 off, the earlier results. On the GPU
# 1 needs the fused path (imex_pcg_start 2 or 3, imex_pcg_fused 1, imex_warm
# 1, imex_gpu_stage, imex_gpu_sweep and imex_gpu_redu on: the defaults);
# otherwise the run stops at start-up and asks for imex_corr_adv = 0.
# imex_corr_adv_clip (ucla-roms #451, 0b7a1403; a solver setting on both
# codes, not in the template): with imex_corr_adv = 1, the largest
# Courant number of the face velocity that the advective buoyancy change
# X commands in a cell through the cell's own along-level coupling; |X|
# is clipped per cell to that cap, set at each operator build. 0.1 is the
# default, 0 turns the clip off (the earlier results), a value < 0 stops
# the run at start-up. Where no cell is clipped results are the same as
# with 0. imex_verbose >= 1 prints IMEX_CLIP lines (clipped and active
# cell-steps since the last line) at each operator build and at the end
# of the run, as on the CPU.
# imex_bref_trigger (ucla-roms #456, e62b3b17; a solver
# setting on both codes, not in the template): b_ref, the operator and
# its preconditioner are also rebuilt at the next step when the exposure
# E of some column (not within two cells of an open edge) to the stale
# b_ref exceeds this and b_ref is at least 1 h old; imex_bref_hours
# stays the longest age. E: the explicit residual stratification
# N2(b*) - N2(b_ref) projected on the column's three fastest WKB modes
# of the operator's N2, against the operator's N2 on the mode, weighted
# by W^2/(W^2 + 2) (W the mode's grid-scale Courant number), as a
# fraction of x_inf, the stiff-mode limit of the time-step weights in
# effect (0.3096 for the default weights; printed at start-up). 0.646
# (e = 0.2 with the default weights) is the default, 0 rebuilds never on
# demand (the earlier results), a value < 0 stops the run at start-up.
# E is computed every step at every imex_verbose: IMEX_BREF_DEMAND lines
# at each demand, IMEX_BREF_E lines at each rebuild (reason, b_ref age,
# largest E since the last rebuild), after each IMEX line (imex_verbose
# >= 1) and at the end of the run, as on the CPU. Restarts stay exact
# (the age is in the restart file) and the demand steps do not depend on
# the tiling (one MPI max of one number per step).
# imex_pc ('modes', the default on both codes since ucla-roms branch
# imex-pc-modes-default, 8c1d6909; it was 'jacobi' before; 'jacobi'),
# imex_pc_modes (0 automatic, the
# default; 1-4), imex_pc_cou_on (0.5), imex_pc_cou_k (0.3), imex_pc_levels (0
# automatic, 2, 3), imex_pc_ncoarse (2; 1, 2), imex_pc_smoother ('rbgs';
# 'jacobi') and imex_pc_dump (only 0 on the GPU): the mode-split
# preconditioner of the stage solves (ucla-roms branch imex-pc-modes,
# bf897292), the same keys, defaults and checks; IMEX_PCM lines at each
# operator rebuild. With imex_pc_modes = 0 it is the Jacobi path wherever
# it builds no modes (K 0), so those runs are unchanged. On the GPU 'modes'
# needs the same fused path as imex_corr_adv (the defaults); otherwise the
# run stops at start-up and asks for imex_pc = 'jacobi' (on the CPU, the
# diagnostic settings imex_pcg_start 0 or 1, imex_selftest 1 and imex_redu 1
# with imex_pcg_fused 0 stop the same way).
# GPU tuning settings (roms_gpu only; a namelist that
# sets one stops UCLA ROMS): imex_gpu_redu, imex_gpu_stage, imex_gpu_sweep
# (on: deterministic sums, the fused stage, the restructured operator sweep),
# and imex_gpu_timers (timing runs: 0 off, the default; 1 and 2 print IMEX_WIN
# lines with synchronised windows of the IMEX step, the stage windows on the
# fused path; results are the same at 0, 1 and 2). 'modal' needs the fused
# solve (imex_pcg_start 2 or 3, imex_pcg_fused 1, imex_warm 1) with
# imex_gpu_stage and imex_gpu_sweep on (the defaults); with other values
# 'modal' stops and 'auto' runs 'fixed' with a note (the CPU would run
# 'modal', e.g. with imex_pcg_start 0).
# Keys removed from UCLA ROMS on 2026-11-13 (their former defaults are now
# fixed) stop the run at the read with a message that lists them; this
# GNU sed line deletes them, with their comment and value continuation
# lines, from a namelist file (the same line as in UCLA ROMS's
# src/namelist.nml):
